    "title": "Could the Chicago area see a lunar eclipse and the Northern Lights this week? - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By NBC Chicago Staff ,\n10 hours ago A pair of unique events could occur in the skies over the Chicago area this week, but will residents be able to see them?. Thursday night will see a full moon rise over the Chicago area, and with it will come a partial lunar eclipse, with nearly 96% of the moon’s surface covered by the Earth’s shadow, according to NASA. Read full article",
